; Sprites: coil (4 frames), fringed dome (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B900+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like a twisting figure-eight or coil; frames 4-7 look
; like a checkered dome with a fringe underneath. Used by entity definitions $0E $3B $3E $5D in rooms $01 $09 $16 $21.
@label=SpritesCoilDome
